1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,333
Can options information help forecast stock movement?

2
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:06,667
Forecast 15-minute variance, not price direction.

3
00:00:06,667 --> 00:00:10,000
Compare three information sets at the same origins.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,333
Stock bars provide the six stocks' price histories.

5
00:00:13,333 --> 00:00:16,667
Option identities link quotes and activity to underlying, type, strike and expiry.

6
00:00:16,667 --> 00:00:20,000
SPY and QQQ: market context and a separate ETF extension.

7
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Options source timestamps must precede origin t by at least 120 seconds.

8
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
This assumes availability; customer receipt was not observed.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Subsequent realized variance scores the forecast. It never enters its predictors.

10
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
B0: 29 predictors. Add option state for B1: 69 total.

11
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Add mixed activity, price changes, exposure proxies and coverage: B2 has 138 predictors.

12
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Both linear and tree families fit all three information sets.

13
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Training and tuning use eligible history before each evaluation.

14
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Pair losses at identical origins; average within each asset-session.

15
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Equal asset and session averages yield 419 calendar sessions—not independent ticks.

16
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Option state improves both families in this historical sample.

17
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Mixed B2: linear loss reduction 0.623%; trees -0.115%.

18
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
QLIKE loss reductions are not investment returns or causal evidence.

19
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Final 25 sessions: no confirmation. Linear H2 nominal p = 0.1758.

20
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Assumed source-time cutoffs change the estimated gain substantially.

21
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Shuffling retains 81.63% of mean gain; timely flow is not isolated.

22
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,333
Research overview → evidence map → public tables and figures.

23
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:26,667
Clone, install the locked environment, then recreate published figures.

24
00:01:26,667 --> 00:01:30,000
Next, verify public evidence. A raw-data rebuild requires licensed inputs.
